{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-342229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}-y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}} & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & \\,-(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & \\,\\,=-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}-{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}-{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,=-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the coefficients next to sines and cosines, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-1 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}-{a}_{n}=\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi } \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}-{b}_{n}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=2,$ which means the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, from the third equation, ${b}_{n}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}.$ Substituting this into the third equation, gives\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2})\\frac{n\\pi }{2}-{a}_{n}=\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{16}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{16}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼1 & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{16}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{8}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "780dcc0827b7cc928c082b0b4b7b45ad18ea474c27524d9603b01ad71c22a1bf"} {"question" "q-342229" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342229" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342229" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342229" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" 