{162}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}-2y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}} & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,-2(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,\\,=-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -2\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-2{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-2{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,=-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the coefficients next to sines and cosines, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-2{a}_{n}=\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi } \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-2{b}_{n}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=2,$ which means the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, from the third equation, ${b}_{n}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{6}.$ Substituting this into the third equation, gives\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{6})\\frac{n\\pi }{3}-2{a}_{n}=\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{72}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{6}\\cdot (-\\frac{72}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼1 & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{72}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{12}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "780dcc0827b7cc928c082b0b4b7b45ad18ea474c27524d9603b01ad71c22a1bf"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{24}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] ["math" "-\\frac{72}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] ["math" "\\frac{36}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{72}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{12}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] ["math" "\\frac{24}{{n}^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343854" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}-5y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}} & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,-5(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,\\,=-5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -5\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-5{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-5{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,=-5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the coefficients next to sines and cosines, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-5 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-5{a}_{n}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-5{b}_{n}=\\frac{2(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=2,$ which means the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, from the second equation, ${b}_{n}=\\frac{15{a}_{n}}{n\\pi }.$ Substituting this into the third equation, gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-5(\\frac{15{a}_{n}}{n\\pi })=\\frac{2(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{15{a}_{n}}{n\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225} \\\\  & =\\frac{90(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼1 & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{90(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "780dcc0827b7cc928c082b0b4b7b45ad18ea474c27524d9603b01ad71c22a1bf"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225}"] ["math" "\\frac{30(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225}"] ["math" "\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{90(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}"] ["math" "\\frac{18(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}"] ["math" "\\frac{90(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343860" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{90(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+225)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}+5y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))+{b}_{n}\\cdot n\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)) \\\\  & \\,+5(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)) \\\\  & \\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{5{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({b}_{n}n\\pi +5{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-{a}_{n}n\\pi +5{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the cosine and sine coefficients, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{a}_{0}}{2}=0 \\\\ {b}_{n}n\\pi +5{a}_{n}=0 \\\\ -{a}_{n}n\\pi +5{b}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nNext, from the second equation, \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the third equation gives\n\n$$\n-(-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{5})n\\pi +5{b}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{5}\\cdot \\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "780dcc0827b7cc928c082b0b4b7b45ad18ea474c27524d9603b01ad71c22a1bf"} {"question" "q-342203" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342203" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}"] ["math" "\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342203" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342203" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342203" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{25(-1)^{n}}{n{\\pi }^{2}(n\\pi +5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi (n\\pi +5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-342203" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-3y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that all the sine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})-3(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))=3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n-3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{9}-3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})=3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=3 \\\\ {a}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{9}-3)=\\frac{3(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-1 \\\\ {a}_{n}=\\frac{27(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+27)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{27(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+27)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "780dcc0827b7cc928c082b0b4b7b45ad18ea474c27524d9603b01ad71c22a1bf"} {"question" "q-343880" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343880" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343880" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074986/state.json" "file_sha256" "98cd9a0d00664aad6bd9b61b1f95ba7af238532b160bbb9c07501e577ada2b6a"} {"question" "q-343880" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma